  "worked_solution": "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe start by factoring the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =P-0.000\\,5{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.000\\,5P(2\\,000-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,5,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=2\\,000.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{2\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(2\\,000\\cdot 0.000\\,5)t}}=\\frac{2\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=2$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =2 \\\\ \\frac{2\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(0)}} & =2 \\\\ 1+C & =1\\,000 \\\\ C & =999\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{2\\,000}{1+999{e}^{-t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=7$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5) & =\\frac{2\\,000}{1+999{e}^{-7}} \\\\  & \u22481047.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $7$ hours, approximately $1047$ students have heard the rumor.",
